# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 227-230 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, 2026-09-25): the nest by chance, even one egg, the orchard's geese,
# the way, the tree, the ground, the viable and the flying, the sitting mother, one kind, not even for the leper (227 — its eleventh English row misplaced);
# the sending five times, the orchard and the house, the clean bird by the prototype (228 — 228:5 REREAD WHOLE from chapter 14), females not males, the male
# partridge, R. Judah's lashes and the Mishnah's pointer; the house however acquired, the sheds, the dwelling, the pits and the Sanctuary, three and ten
# handbreadths, the faller who deserved it, from it not into it, R. Ishmael's fish, the four-by-four house (229); the vineyard's mixed seed — two prohibitions,
# a single vine, forbidden for benefit by the analogy, the rooting and the white bean, the wind, the thorns, others' vineyards, the tendril of a hundred cubits,
# the ox and the ass together (230). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(227, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF A NEST CHANCE" (22:6) — EXCLUDING THE READY AT HAND. The head row of piska 227 ({SP_(227, 1, "פרט", "למזמן")} "excluding the ready at hand"): the nest\'s law on the CHANCE find alone — the domesticated bird excluded (Chullin 12:1 the answer sheet); the compile\'s condition. Fresh.')
srow(227, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LEAST OF "FLEDGLINGS" IS TWO, THE LEAST OF "EGGS" TWO; WHENCE THAT WITH ONE FLEDGLING OR ONE EGG HE MUST SEND HER? "A NEST" — A NEST OF ANY NUMBER. ({SP_(227, 2, "מעוט", "אפרוחים", "שנים")} "the least of fledglings — two"; {SP_(227, 2, "קן", "מכל", "מקום")} "a nest — from anywhere"): THE COUNT PARAMETER — the plural\'s minimum two overridden by "nest": even one (Chullin 12:3). Fresh.')
srow(227, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM "ON THE WAY … THE MOTHER SITTING ON THE FLEDGLINGS OR THE EGGS" MIGHT I EXCLUDE GEESE AND HENS THAT NESTED IN THE ORCHARD? "BEFORE YOU". ({SP_(227, 3, "אוזים", "ותרנגולים", "שקננו", "בפרדס")} "geese and hens that nested in the orchard"): the orchard\'s escaped fowl inside the law by "before you" (228:2 the ruling) — the domestication boundary. Fresh.')
srow(227, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY IN A PRIVATE DOMAIN? THE PUBLIC DOMAIN FROM "ON THE WAY". ({SP_(227, 4, "ברשות", "הרבים", "מנין")} "in the public domain — whence?"): the place — every domain. Fresh.')
srow(227, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ON THE TREES — WHENCE? "IN ANY TREE". ({SP_(227, 5, "על", "האילנות", "מנין")} "on the trees — whence?"): the second place clause; a row citing nothing in either file. Fresh.')
srow(227, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ON THE GROUND — WHENCE? "OR ON THE GROUND". ({SP_(227, 6, "על", "הארץ", "מנין")} "on the ground — whence?"): the third place clause — the verse\'s three places read one by one. Fresh.')
srow(227, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE MOTHER SITTING ON THE FLEDGLINGS OR ON THE EGGS" — AS FLEDGLINGS ARE VIABLE, SO EGGS VIABLE: THE ADDLED EXCLUDED; AS EGGS NEED THEIR MOTHER, SO FLEDGLINGS NEED THEIR MOTHER: THE FLIERS EXCLUDED. ({SP_(227, 7, "יצאו", "מוזרות")} "the addled are excluded"; {SP_(227, 7, "יצאו", "המפריחים")} "the fliers are excluded"): the two exclusions by the pair\'s mutual measure — the young\'s STATE a parameter (Chullin 12:3). Fresh.')
srow(227, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE MOTHER SITTING" — WHEN SHE SITS ON THEM, EXCLUDING THE HOVERING; EVEN WITH HER WINGS TOUCHING THE NEST? "THE MOTHER SITTING ON THE FLEDGLINGS" — EVEN THOUGH SHE IS NOT WITH THEM. ({SP_(227, 8, "פרט", "למעופפת")} "excluding the hovering one"): the mother\'s POSTURE the condition — sitting, not flying; the touch of the wings enough (Chullin 12:3). Fresh.')
srow(227, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'AN UNCLEAN BIRD SITTING ON A CLEAN BIRD\'S EGGS, A CLEAN ON AN UNCLEAN\'S — MUST HE SEND? "THE MOTHER SITTING" — UNTIL ALL ARE ONE KIND. ({SP_(227, 9, "עד", "שיהיו", "כלם", "מין", "אחד")} "until they are all one kind"): the kind\'s identity a condition (Chullin 12:2). Fresh.')
srow(227, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"TAKE NOT THE MOTHER WITH THE YOUNG" — FROM "THE PRIEST SHALL TAKE FOR THE ONE PURIFIED TWO LIVING CLEAN BIRDS" (Leviticus 14:4) MIGHT HE TAKE HER TO PURIFY THE LEPER? "TAKE NOT THE MOTHER" — NOT EVEN TO PURIFY THE LEPER. ({SP_(227, 10, "אפלו", "לטהר", "בה", "את", "המצורע")} "even to purify the leper with her"): THE LEPER\'S BIRDS BARRED FROM THE NEST — the metzora rite\'s CALL on the nest\'s mother refused (Chullin 12:5); a cross-daemon condition. Fresh.')
srow(227, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"TAKE NOT THE MOTHER" — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(227, 11, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the prohibition\'s seat. THE ENGLISH ROW IS MISPLACED — the export\'s 227:11 in the English carries 229:9\'s text (R. Ishmael\'s fish, Ecclesiastes 9:12) and not this row\'s: the Hebrew is read, the English file\'s row noted as the export\'s slip. Fresh.')
srow(228, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SURELY SEND" (22:7) — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT; SENT HER AND SHE RETURNED, SENT HER AND SHE RETURNED, EVEN FIVE TIMES — HE MUST SEND. The head row of piska 228 ({SP_(228, 1, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"; {SP_(228, 1, "אפלו", "חמש", "פעמים")} "even five times"): the doubled verb\'s repetition as at 222:8 and 225:6 — three "five times" in the two piskaot. Fresh.')
srow(228, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'GEESE AND HENS THAT REBELLED AND NESTED IN THE ORCHARD — HE MUST SEND; IN THE HOUSE — EXEMPT FROM SENDING. ({SP_(228, 2, "שמרדו", "ושקננו", "בפרדס")} "that rebelled and nested in the orchard"; {SP_(228, 2, "בבית", "פטור", "מלשלח")} "in the house — exempt from sending"): THE DOMESTICATION BOUNDARY ruled — the escaped fowl wild again, the house-nest exempt; 227:3\'s question answered. Fresh.')
srow(228, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FLEDGLINGS OR EGGS" — AS FLEDGLINGS HAVE USE, THE DEAD EXCLUDED; SO EGGS WITH USE, THE ADDLED EXCLUDED; THE LEAST TWO, EVEN ONE — HE MUST SEND; ANOTHER WORD: "IF A NEST CHANCE BEFORE YOU" — ANYWHERE. ({SP_(228, 3, "יצאו", "מתים")} "the dead are excluded"; {SP_(228, 3, "מכל", "מקום")} "from anywhere"): 227:2-3 reprised in short (the translator: a condensed reprise, thinly attested) — the young\'s use the measure. Fresh.')
srow(228, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON THE WAY, IN ANY TREE OR ON THE GROUND" — AS THE WAY IS FREE, THE TIED BIRDS IN ANOTHER\'S DOMAIN ARE EXCLUDED. ({SP_(228, 4, "יצאו", "מקשרים")} "the tied are excluded"): the bird\'s freedom the condition — the tied bird owned. Fresh.')
srow(228, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "SURELY SEND" — OF A CLEAN BIRD; OR EVEN AN UNCLEAN? "EVERY CLEAN BIRD YOU SHALL EAT" (14:11) — THIS IS A PROTOTYPE: WHEREVER "BIRD" IS SAID, THE CLEAN IS MEANT, AS R. JOSIAH; IF HE SENT HER AND TURNED HIS FACE ON THE WAY — EXEMPT FROM SENDING. ({SP_(228, 5, "זה", "בנין", "אב")} "this is a prototype"; {SP_(228, 5, "בטהורה", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of the clean the verse speaks"): THE PROTOTYPE (I3) from chapter 14\'s clean bird — "bird" means clean throughout the Torah; the nest\'s law on clean birds only; the sender who walked on exempt. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 14, deu_14_reeh).')
srow(228, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"SURELY SEND" — OF FEMALES THE VERSE SPEAKS, NOT OF MALES. ({SP_(228, 6, "בנקבות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of females the verse speaks"): "the mother" the sex parameter. Fresh.')
srow(228, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'A MALE PARTRIDGE — R. ELIEZER OBLIGATES THE SENDING, "SURELY SEND"; THE SAGES EXEMPT, "THE MOTHER" — EXCLUDING THE MALE PARTRIDGE. ({SP_(228, 7, "פרט", "לקורא", "זכר")} "excluding the male partridge"): the brooding male a DISPUTED cell (Chullin 12:2) — the sages\' exemption the answer sheet\'s. Fresh.')
srow(228, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE WHO TAKES THE MOTHER FROM THE YOUNG — R. JUDAH SAYS: HE IS FLOGGED AND DOES NOT SEND; THE SAGES SAY: HE SENDS AND IS NOT FLOGGED — "AND SO ON, THE MISHNAH, UNTIL \'THE WEIGHTY COMMANDMENTS OF THE TORAH\'". ({SP_(228, 8, "לוקה", "ואינו", "משלח")} "flogged and does not send"; {SP_(228, 8, "מצוות", "חמורות", "שבתורה")} "the weighty commandments of the Torah"): THE SPINE POINTS TO THE MISHNAH BY ABBREVIATION — "etc., the Mishnah until …" (Chullin 12:4-5 the answer sheet, the lashes and the a fortiori (I1) from the commandment worth an issar (the smallest coin) to the weighty ones) — the answer sheet cited as a text to open, not copied; the compile\'s sanction parameter (a prohibition repaired by an act carries no lashes). Fresh.')
srow(229, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU BUILD A NEW HOUSE" (22:8) — ONLY A BUILDER? ONE WHO BOUGHT, INHERITED, WAS GIVEN — "A HOUSE" ANYWHERE. The head row of piska 229 ({SP_(229, 1, "לקח", "ירש", "ונתן", "לו", "במתנה", "מנין")} "bought, inherited, given as a gift — whence?"): the parapet\'s duty on every owner — 194:1\'s words for the war exemption\'s new house (20:5), the twin. Fresh.')
srow(229, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"PUT NOT BLOOD IN YOUR HOUSE" — ONLY A HOUSE? THE STRAW HOUSE, THE CATTLE HOUSE, THE WOOD HOUSE, THE STOREHOUSES — "PUT NOT BLOOD IN YOUR HOUSE". ({SP_(229, 2, "בית", "התבן", "בית", "הבקר")} "the straw house, the cattle house"): the duty widened to every roofed building by the blood clause. Fresh.')
srow(229, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'EVEN A GATEHOUSE, A PORTICO, A BALCONY? "HOUSE" — AS A HOUSE IS A DWELLING, THESE ARE EXCLUDED, NOT DWELLINGS. ({SP_(229, 3, "שהוא", "בית", "דירה")} "which is a dwelling house"): the dwelling the class\'s mark — the unroofed and the open excluded. Fresh.')
srow(229, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"MAKE A PARAPET FOR YOUR ROOF" — ONLY A ROOF? PITS, DITCHES, CAVES, TRENCHES — "PUT NOT BLOOD IN YOUR HOUSE"; WHY "ROOF"? EXCLUDING THE RAMP; "HOUSE" — INCLUDING THE SANCTUARY; "ROOF" — EXCLUDING THE PORCH. ({SP_(229, 4, "פרט", "לכבש")} "excluding the ramp"; {SP_(229, 4, "לרבות", "היכל")} "including the Sanctuary"; {SP_(229, 4, "פרט", "לאולם")} "excluding the porch"): THE TEMPLE INSIDE THE PARAPET LAW — the altar\'s ramp and the porch out, the Sanctuary\'s roof in (Middot 3:5, 4:6-7 the answer sheet); the hazards of the ground under the blood clause. Fresh.')
srow(229, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"NEW" — RABBI SAYS: FROM THE TIME OF ITS NEWNESS MAKE IT A PARAPET; HOW HIGH? WHERE THEY ROLL, THREE HANDBREADTHS; WHERE THEY TREAD, TEN. ({SP_(229, 5, "מעגילו", "שלשה", "טפחים")} "its rolling-place three handbreadths"; {SP_(229, 5, "בית", "דרסו", "עשרה")} "its treading-place ten"): THE PARAPET\'S TWO MEASURES — three and ten handbreadths by the roof\'s use — PARAMETERS; the duty from the building\'s day. Fresh.')
srow(229, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"MAKE A PARAPET FOR YOUR ROOF" — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT; "PUT NOT BLOOD IN YOUR HOUSE" — A NEGATIVE ONE. ({SP_(229, 6, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): the pair inside one verse. Fresh.')
srow(229, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THE FALLER FALLS FROM IT" — THIS ONE WAS FIT TO FALL! BUT MERIT IS ROLLED THROUGH THE MERITORIOUS AND GUILT THROUGH THE GUILTY. ({SP_(229, 7, "ראוי", "זה", "שיפול")} "this one was fit to fall"; {SP_(229, 7, "מגלגלים", "זכות", "על", "ידי", "זכי")} "they roll merit through the meritorious"): HEAVEN\'S RECKONING inside the building code — the faller\'s desert and the owner\'s guilt two ledgers (Tosefta Yom Kippur 5:12, Sifrei Numbers 114 the parallels); a heaven entry for the compile. Fresh.')
srow(229, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM IT" — AND NOT INTO IT: IF THE PUBLIC WAY WAS TEN HANDBREADTHS HIGHER AND ONE FELL FROM IT INTO THE HOUSE — EXEMPT, FOR "FROM IT" NOT "INTO IT". ({SP_(229, 8, "ממנו", "ולא", "לתוכו")} "from it and not into it"; {SP_(229, 8, "עשרה", "טפחים")} "ten handbreadths"): the direction of the fall the liability\'s condition — the sunken roof exempt. Fresh.')
srow(229, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHEN YOU BUILD" — R. ISHMAEL SAYS: THE VERSE TEACHES THAT NO MAN KNOWS HOW HE IS JUDGED, AS "MAN KNOWS NOT HIS TIME, LIKE FISH CAUGHT IN A NET" (Ecclesiastes 9:12). ({SP_(229, 9, "שאין", "אדם", "יודע", "כיצד", "הוא", "נדון")} "that no man knows how he is judged"): the homily on the new house — the judgment unknown; no rule. Fresh.')
srow(229, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"HOUSE" — HENCE THEY SAID: A HOUSE WITHOUT FOUR BY FOUR CUBITS IS EXEMPT FROM THE PARAPET, THE DOORPOST SCROLL AND THE COURTYARD\'S JOINING; IT DOES NOT EXTEND THE CITY, DOES NOT BIND PRODUCE TO THE TITHE, GETS NO FOUR CUBITS AT ITS DOOR; ONE WHO VOWS OFF "THE HOUSE" MAY SIT IN IT; IT IS NOT DEFILED BY PLAGUE-SIGNS, DOES NOT REVERT AT THE JUBILEE, AND THE WARRIORS DO NOT RETURN FOR IT. ({SP_(229, 10, "ארבע", "על", "ארבע")} "four by four"; {SP_(229, 10, "פטור", "מן", "המעקה", "ומן", "המזוזה")} "exempt from the parapet and from the doorpost scroll"): THE HOUSE\'S SIZE PARAMETER — four by four cubits — SHARED BY NINE LAWS (the parapet, the doorpost, the Sabbath joining, the city\'s bound, the tithe, the door\'s space, the vow, the house-plague, the Jubilee, the war exemption): one parameter across ten daemons — the compile\'s registry row. Fresh.')
srow(230, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SOW NOT YOUR VINEYARD WITH MIXED SEED" (22:9) — WHY NEEDED, WHEN "YOUR FIELD YOU SHALL NOT SOW WITH MIXED SEED" (Leviticus 19:19) IS SAID? WHOEVER KEEPS MIXED SEED IN A VINEYARD TRANSGRESSES TWO PROHIBITIONS. The head row of piska 230 ({SP_(230, 1, "עובר", "בשני", "לאוים")} "transgresses two prohibitions"): the vineyard\'s seat a second prohibition over the field\'s — the count of transgressions the compile\'s effect (Sifra Kedoshim the parallel). Fresh.')
srow(230, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY A WHOLE VINEYARD? EVEN A SINGLE VINE BEARING FRUIT — "VINEYARD" ANYWHERE. ({SP_(230, 2, "גפן", "יחידי", "ועושה", "פרות")} "a single vine bearing fruit"): the vineyard\'s minimum one vine (Kilayim 4:6 the answer sheet\'s measures). Fresh.')
srow(230, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT THE VINEYARD\'S MIXED SEED IS FORBIDDEN FOR BENEFIT? "SANCTIFIED" IS SAID HERE AND "HOLY" THERE (Leviticus 5:15) — AS THE HOLY THERE IS FORBIDDEN FOR BENEFIT, SO HERE. ({SP_(230, 3, "אסור", "בהניה")} "forbidden for benefit"; {SP_(230, 3, "נאמר", "כאן", "תקדש")} "here it says \'be sanctified\'"): THE VERBAL ANALOGY (I2) on the root "holy" — the trespass offering\'s sanctity teaches the mixture\'s ban on benefit; the effect\'s class (forbidden for benefit, not for eating alone). Fresh.')
srow(230, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST THE FULLNESS OF THE SEED BE SANCTIFIED" — FROM WHEN IS THE SEED SANCTIFIED? FROM ITS ROOTING; AND GRAPES? FROM THEIR BECOMING LIKE A WHITE BEAN. ({SP_(230, 4, "משתשריש")} "from its rooting"; {SP_(230, 4, "כפול", "לבן")} "like a white bean"): THE CLOCK OF THE BAN — the seed\'s rooting and the grape\'s size (Kilayim 7:7 the answer sheet) — two growth parameters. Fresh.')
srow(230, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE SEED" — EXCLUDING SEED THAT WENT OUT WITH THE DUNG OR WITH THE WATER, OR THE SOWER WHOSE SEED THE WIND STORMS; MIGHT I EXCLUDE THE SOWER WHOM THE WIND ASSISTS? "WHICH YOU SOW". ({SP_(230, 5, "עם", "הזבלים", "או", "עם", "המים")} "with the dung or with the water"): the INTENT condition — the unintended sowing out, the wind-helped sowing in (Kilayim 5:7). Fresh.')
srow(230, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE WHO KEEPS THORNS IN A VINEYARD — R. ELIEZER SAYS: SANCTIFIED, FOR "WHICH YOU SOW"; THE SAGES SAY: "SEED" EXCLUDES THE KEEPER OF THORNS. ({SP_(230, 6, "פרט", "למקים", "קוצים", "בכרם")} "excluding one who keeps thorns in a vineyard"): the thorns a DISPUTED cell (Kilayim 5:8) — the sages\' exclusion the answer sheet\'s. Fresh.')
srow(230, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE PRODUCE OF THE VINEYARD" — FROM WHEN IS THE PRODUCE SANCTIFIED? FROM ITS ROOTING; GRAPES FROM THEIR RISING LIKE A WHITE BEAN. ({SP_(230, 7, "משתשריש")} "from its rooting"): 230:4\'s clock read again on the produce clause — one clock for the seed and the vine. Fresh.')
srow(230, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY A FRUIT-BEARING VINEYARD? A BARREN ONE — "VINEYARD" ANYWHERE; ONLY YOUR OWN? OTHERS\' — "SOW NOT YOUR VINEYARD WITH MIXED SEED" ANYWHERE. ({SP_(230, 8, "כרם", "של", "אחרים", "מנין")} "others\' vineyard — whence?"): the scope — barren and another\'s. Fresh.')
srow(230, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE WHO STRETCHES A VINE\'S TENDRIL OVER SEEDS, EVEN A HUNDRED CUBITS — THE VINE AND ITS FRUIT ARE FORBIDDEN. ({SP_(230, 9, "אפלו", "מאה", "אמה")} "even a hundred cubits"): the tendril\'s reach the mixture — a distance parameter with no limit (Tosefta Kilayim 4:10); a row citing nothing in either file. Fresh.')
srow(230, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'["PLOW NOT WITH AN OX AND AN ASS" (22:10) —] NOT WITH THIS ONE ALONE AND THAT ONE ALONE? "TOGETHER" — EACH ALONE IS PERMITTED. ({SP_(230, 10, "תלמוד", "לומר", "יחדו")} "the Teaching says: together"): 22:10 read inside piska 230 before its own piska 231 — "together" the condition, the single beast free. Fresh.')
srow(230, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MIXED SEED" — TO MAKE LIABLE ON ACCOUNT OF THE VINEYARD AND ON ACCOUNT OF THE FIELD. ({SP_(230, 11, "משום", "כרם", "ומשום", "שדה")} "on account of the vineyard and on account of the field"): 230:1\'s two prohibitions named from the word itself. Fresh.')
srow(230, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "LEST THE FULLNESS BE SANCTIFIED" — LEST THE FULLNESS BE FORBIDDEN, AS R. JOSIAH. ({SP_(230, 12, "פן", "תאסר", "המלאה")} "lest the fullness be forbidden"): the word "sanctified" glossed "forbidden" — the verb\'s sense the effect\'s (230:3\'s analogy in one word). Fresh.')
srow(230, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOU SOW" — ONLY WHAT HE SOWED? HIS FELLOW SOWED AND HE WISHES TO KEEP IT — "YOU SOW" ANYWHERE. ({SP_(230, 13, "זרע", "חבירו", "ורצה", "לקימו")} "his fellow sowed and he wished to keep it"): the keeper liable as the sower — maintaining is sowing. Fresh.')
